<title>INDIA: India soybean prices steady in thin, holiday trade.</title>
<headline>India soybean prices steady in thin, holiday trade.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Friday were steady in thin, holiday trade in local markets, dealers said.</p>
<p>Most central Indian markets are closed for a Moslem festival. Business volumes were dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained firm on limited supplies. Prices were up by 300 rupees per tonne. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady. Soymeal yellow was $265-268 rupees per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for exports. Rapeseed extraction was $97-100 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,300 rupees to 3,400 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free rail condition).</p>
